    "summary": "Cushion cover. Single rectangle of cotton batik cloth, half unpatterned, half of Javanese workmanship but some design elements apparently European.  Border of zig-zags, main motif a version of a sawat with a kind of surrounding wreath.  Reddish brown ground, dotted in main square with six green trifoliate shapes set against it.  Band defining wreath shape is blue with inner dotted white line, the rest in cream and green.   [Text written by Dr Fiona Kerlogue, Horniman Museum.]",
